{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957410-dread-horrors-in-a-song-of-ice-and-fire","id":957410,"title":"Dread Horrors in a Song of Ice and Fire.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T22:09:47-07:00","id":957410,"title":"Dread Horrors in a Song of Ice and Fire.","content":"I really would like to run a personal horror game using CofD for ASOIF world. The tricky part is coming up with a monster or supernatural threat that feels like it could fit well into the world. What sort of unique horror or that would fit in this world. I have one, and will write it up in detail tomorrow if this thread gets any traction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T08:01:30-07:00","id":957624,"title":"","content":"Well, for faithful, detail representations, invoking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> is usually a good bet.<br /> <br /> Are you aiming to convert The Others (alt. White Walkers) over into CofD Horrors? As well as the other odd magic peoples and bits.<br /> <br /> ASoIaF is very &quot;low&quot; magic, so I don't see the need for anything other than Supernatural Merits, Micro-templates, and Horrors, really. Might want to dig out some of the vampire books for their politics, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T05:21:30-07:00","id":967273,"title":"","content":"As an idea, could the thing beneath the temple of the Warlocks be a part of this? I'm not sure where, but I remember there being something down there that the Warlocks deal with, connecting their minds to it and sustaining it with food in return for it providing them immortality (of a sort) and their particular brand of magic. The impressions I can remember from the descriptions were something along the lines of something made of age and dust and wrinkled skin like ancient parchment. Sounds interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:56:10-07:00","id":967374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957410-dread-horrors-in-a-song-of-ice-and-fire?p=967273#post967273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an idea, could the thing beneath the temple of the Warlocks be a part of this? I'm not sure where, but I remember there being something down there that the Warlocks deal with, connecting their minds to it and sustaining it with food in return for it providing them immortality (of a sort) and their particular brand of magic. The impressions I can remember from the descriptions were something along the lines of something made of age and dust and wrinkled skin like ancient parchment. Sounds interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The warlocks seemed able to keep more of their power in the house of the undying. Knowing grrm's many others stories, it seemed to be a thin point between realities. They Undying themselves had some resemblance to Auspex vampires in a semi torpor state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:01:50-07:00","id":967378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957410-dread-horrors-in-a-song-of-ice-and-fire?p=957624#post957624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for faithful, detail representations, invoking <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> is usually a good bet.<br /> <br /> Are you aiming to convert The Others (alt. White Walkers) over into CofD Horrors? As well as the other odd magic peoples and bits.<br /> <br /> ASoIaF is very &quot;low&quot; magic, so I don't see the need for anything other than Supernatural Merits, Micro-templates, and Horrors, really. Might want to dig out some of the vampire books for their politics, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like most of the supernatural creatures in asofiaf are unique, unless you mean the others coftf, stone men and squishers. The shrowded lord, rat cook, biter, bloodraven, the chimeric creatures on southoros, and the undying would probably need to use the dread horror rules, but I would give the races their own simplified splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:01:43-07:00","id":973112,"title":"","content":"I'm sure Bloodraven works just fine with some psychic merits on an ordinary human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:17:20-07:00","id":973122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tambov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957410-dread-horrors-in-a-song-of-ice-and-fire?p=973112#post973112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure Bloodraven works just fine with some psychic merits on an ordinary human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think not, because even if you killed his body, he is in the trees, and the rocks, and the animals. He might even be able to move his concousness to another person permenatly, since he is more experianced than Bran. He can see all the way across the world to Asshai, and effect peoples dreams from contients away. You could pretty much look at him as the AOIAF version of a one man illuminati.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:30:53-07:00","id":973130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957410-dread-horrors-in-a-song-of-ice-and-fire?p=973122#post973122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think not, because even if you killed his body, he is in the trees, and the rocks, and the animals. He might even be able to move his concousness to another person permenatly, since he is more experianced than Bran. He can see all the way across the world to Asshai, and effect peoples dreams from contients away. You could pretty much look at him as the AOIAF version of a one man illuminati.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possession and/or Astral Projection Supernatural Merit, Clairvoyance, and maybe some Dream merit.<br /> <br /> You could model him as a Body Thief (Psychic) from 1E without much issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T09:29:04-07:00","id":973174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/957410-dread-horrors-in-a-song-of-ice-and-fire?p=973130#post973130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possession and/or Astral Projection Supernatural Merit, Clairvoyance, and maybe some Dream merit.<br /> <br /> You could model him as a Body Thief (Psychic) from 1E without much issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I only have 2nd edition stuff. I hope there is a body thief merit in Hurt Locker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:27:26-07:00","id":973215,"title":"","content":"I think the creatures are unique enough that you'd maybe want to use the dread powers system rather than any of the full game templates.<br /> <br /> On a more mechanical level, I think the Primacy rules from Damnation City would adapt well to the cut-throat politics of Westeros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}